        "original_id": "f9f827d5-e069-5cc7-adcb-a5894a29e58b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gaillardia, Browningia, Helenium\n- Taxa: Asteraceae, Helenieae, genera, cacti, flowering plants\n\nFacts:\n- Gaillardia is a genus of flowering plants in the sunflower family Asteraceae and is native to North and South America.\n- Gaillardia has the common name blanket flower.\n- Browningia is a genus of cacti with 11 accepted species and 3 unresolved species.\n- Helenieae is a tribe whose type genus is Helenium.\n- Gaillardia includes the best known members of the tribe Helenieae.",
